Zoom controls read the viewer from context. Every change eases (unless `smoothZoom` is off) and keeps the page centred, or the point under the cursor once pages are wider than the view.

<Demo example="zoom" height={460} />

## Anatomy

```svelte
<Zoom.Out />
<Zoom.Select />                <!-- fit modes + steps -->
<Zoom.In />
<Zoom.Mode mode="page-width">Width</Zoom.Mode>
```

## Usage

`Zoom.In` and `Zoom.Out` are disabled at the ends of `zoomSteps`, at the viewer's `minZoom` / `maxZoom`, and while `zoomLocked` is set; `Zoom.Mode` exposes `data-active` and `aria-pressed`. For a slider, bind it to the viewer: `bind:value={() => viewer.zoom, (z) => viewer.zoomTo(z)}`.

